    "q-94834": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94834",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(-3.7,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X\\ge -1.1)=0.2578,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2}.$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ | $\\,0.7088\\,$ | $\\,0.7123\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ | $\\,0.7422\\,$ | $\\,0.7454\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1.1) & =1-P(X>-1.1) \\\\  & =1-0.2578 \\\\  & =0.7422\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1.1) & =0.7422 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{-1.1+3.7}{\\sigma }) & =0.7422 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{2.6}{\\sigma }) & =0.7422 \\\\ \\frac{2.6}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7422)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.65)=0.7422\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7422)=0.65.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2.6}{\\sigma } & =0.65 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2.6}{0.65} \\\\ \\sigma  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2}={4}^{2}=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
