    "q-340869": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340869",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(1,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X<-1)=0.3085,$ use the table to find $\\sigma .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.2743\\,$ | $\\,0.2709\\,$ | $\\,0.2676\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.3085\\,$ | $\\,0.3050\\,$ | $\\,0.3015\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3446\\,$ | $\\,0.3409\\,$ | $\\,0.3372\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-1)=0.3085\\,⇒\\,P(X\\le -1)=0.3085\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1) & =0.3085 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{-1-1}{\\sigma }) & =0.3085 \\\\ Φ\\,(-\\frac{2}{\\sigma }) & =0.3085 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.3085)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.50)=0.3085\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.3085)=-0.50.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sigma } & =-0.50 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{2}{0.50} \\\\ \\sigma  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
