    "q-94886": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94886",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(|X|<7)=0.4648,$ find $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6950\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ | $\\,0.7357\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express the given probability as\n\n$$\nP(|X|<7)=P(-7<X<7).\n$$\n\nThen, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-7<X<7) & =0.4648 \\\\ 2P(0<X<7) & =0.4648 \\\\ P(0<X<7) & =0.2324 \\\\ P(X<7)-P(X<0) & =0.2324 \\\\ P(X<7)-0.5 & =0.2324 \\\\ P(X<7) & =0.7324 \\\\ P(X\\le 7) & =0.7324\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 7) & =0.7324 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{7-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.7324 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{7}{\\sigma }) & =0.7324 \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7324)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.62)=0.7324\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7324)=0.62.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{\\sigma } & =0.62 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{7}{0.62} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈11.29.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
