    "q-341990": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341990",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-3<X<3)=0.7888,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ \n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.8925\\,$ | $\\,0.8944\\,$ | $\\,0.8962\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.9099\\,$ | $\\,0.9115\\,$ | $\\,0.9131\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9251\\,$ | $\\,0.9265\\,$ | $\\,0.9279\\,$ |\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-3<X<3) & =0.7888 \\\\ 2P(0<X<3) & =0.7888 \\\\ P(0<X<3) & =0.3944 \\\\ P(X<3)-P(X<0) & =0.3944 \\\\ P(X<3)-0.5 & =0.3944 \\\\ P(X<3) & =0.8944 \\\\ P(X\\le 3) & =0.8944\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.8944 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{3-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.8944 \\\\ Φ\\,(\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.8944 \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.8944)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(1.25)=0.8944\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.8944)=1.25.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =1.25 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3}{1.25} \\\\ \\sigma  & =2.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =(2.4)^{2}=5.76.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
