    "q-94522": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94522",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-3<X<3)=0.9232,$ find ${\\sigma }^{2},$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9418\\,$ | $\\,0.9429\\,$ | $\\,0.9441\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9525\\,$ | $\\,0.9535\\,$ | $\\,0.9545\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9616\\,$ | $\\,0.9625\\,$ | $\\,0.9633\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-3<X<3) & =0.9232 \\\\ 2P(0<X<3) & =0.9232 \\\\ P(0<X<3) & =0.4616 \\\\ P(X<3)-P(X<0) & =0.4616 \\\\ P(X<3)-0.5 & =0.4616 \\\\ P(X<3) & =0.9616 \\\\ P(X\\le 3) & =0.9616\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =0.9616 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{3-0}{\\sigma }) & =0.9616 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{3}{\\sigma }) & =0.9616 \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.9616)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(1.77)=0.9616\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.9616)=1.77.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sigma } & =1.77 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{3}{1.77} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈1.694\\,92.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =(1.694\\,92)^{2} \\\\  & ≈2.87.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
