    "q-94897": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94897",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(3,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-1<X<7)=0.5346,$ find  $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6950\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ | $\\,0.7357\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $-1<X<7$ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu =3.$*",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that the given interval is symmetric about the mean:\n\n$$\nP(-1<X<7)=P(3-4<X<3+4)\n$$\n\nSo, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1<X<7) & =0.5346 \\\\ 2P(3<X<7) & =0.5346 \\\\ P(3<X<7) & =0.2673 \\\\ P(X<7)-P(X<3) & =0.2673 \\\\ P(X<7)-0.5 & =0.2673 \\\\ P(X<7) & =0.7673 \\\\ P(X\\le 7) & =0.7673\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 7) & =0.7673 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{7-3}{\\sigma }) & =0.7673 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{4}{\\sigma }) & =0.7673 \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.7673)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.73)=0.7673\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.7673)=0.73.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\sigma } & =0.73 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{4}{0.73} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈5.479\\,45 \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈5.48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
