    "q-276251": {
      "dom_id": "step-q276251",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(3,{\\sigma }^{2})$ is a normal random variable with $P(-1<X<7)=0.8948,$ use the table to find  $\\sigma ,$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9345\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ | $\\,0.9370\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ | $\\,0.9484\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9564\\,$ | $\\,0.9573\\,$ | $\\,0.9582\\,$ |\n\n*Hint: Note that the interval $-1<X<7$ is symmetric about the mean $\\mu =3.$*\n\n$\\sigma ≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that the given interval is symmetric about the mean:\n\n$$\nP(-1<X<7)=P(3-4<X<3+4)\n$$\n\nSo, we find the cumulative probability using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1<X<7) & =0.8948 \\\\ 2P(3<X<7) & =0.8948 \\\\ P(3<X<7) & =0.4474 \\\\ P(X<7)-P(X<3) & =0.4474 \\\\ P(X<7)-0.5 & =0.4474 \\\\ P(X<7) & =0.9474 \\\\ P(X\\le 7) & =0.9474\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 7) & =0.9474 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{7-3}{\\sigma }) & =0.9474 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{4}{\\sigma }) & =0.9474 \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.9474)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(1.62)=0.9474\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.9474)=1.62.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\sigma } & =1.62 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{4}{1.62} \\\\ \\sigma  & ≈2.47.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
